{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Cost Analysis for Model Optimization\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook analyzes the cost implications of various model optimization techniques we've explored in this workshop, including:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Quantization\n",
    "2. Pruning\n",
    "3. Knowledge Distillation\n",
    "4. Fine-tuning\n",
    "\n",
    "We'll compare the costs of training, inference, and storage for each approach and calculate the potential ROI."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Install required packages\n",
    "!pip install -q \"boto3>=1.26.0\" \"pandas>=1.5.0\" \"numpy>=1.23.0\" \"matplotlib>=3.6.0\" \"seaborn>=0.12.0\" \"tabulate>=0.9.0\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Import required libraries\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import json\n",
    "import boto3\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from tabulate import tabulate\n",
    "from datetime import datetime, timedelta\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set plot style\n",
    "sns.set_style(\"whitegrid\")\n",
    "plt.rcParams[\"figure.figsize\"] = (12, 8)\n",
    "plt.rcParams[\"font.size\"] = 12"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Define Cost Parameters\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's define the cost parameters for different AWS services and instance types used in our workshop."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Define AWS instance costs (per hour in USD)\n",
    "instance_costs = {\n",
    "    \"ml.t3.medium\": 0.05,      # Notebook instance\n",
    "    \"ml.t3.large\": 0.09,       # Notebook instance\n",
    "    \"ml.t3.xlarge\": 0.18,      # Notebook instance\n",
    "    \"ml.m5.large\": 0.115,      # CPU training/inference\n",
    "    \"ml.m5.xlarge\": 0.23,      # CPU training/inference\n",
    "    \"ml.m5.2xlarge\": 0.46,     # CPU training/inference\n",
    "    \"ml.c5.xlarge\": 0.19,      # CPU compute optimized\n",
    "    \"ml.c5.2xlarge\": 0.38,     # CPU compute optimized\n",
    "    \"ml.g4dn.xlarge\": 0.736,   # GPU instance (1 GPU)\n",
    "    \"ml.g4dn.2xlarge\": 0.94,   # GPU instance (1 GPU)\n",
    "    \"ml.g4dn.4xlarge\": 1.505,  # GPU instance (1 GPU)\n",
    "    \"ml.g4dn.8xlarge\": 2.72,   # GPU instance (1 GPU)\n",
    "    \"ml.g4dn.12xlarge\": 4.08,  # GPU instance (4 GPUs)\n",
    "    \"ml.g5.xlarge\": 1.006,     # GPU instance (1 GPU)\n",
    "    \"ml.g5.2xlarge\": 1.212,    # GPU instance (1 GPU)\n",
    "    \"ml.g5.4xlarge\": 1.624,    # GPU instance (1 GPU)\n",
    "    \"ml.g5.8xlarge\": 2.448,    # GPU instance (1 GPU)\n",
    "    \"ml.g5.16xlarge\": 4.896,   # GPU instance (1 GPU)\n",
    "    \"ml.p3.2xlarge\": 3.06,     # GPU instance (1 V100 GPU)\n",
    "    \"ml.p3.8xlarge\": 12.24,    # GPU instance (4 V100 GPUs)\n",
    "    \"ml.p3.16xlarge\": 24.48,   # GPU instance (8 V100 GPUs)\n",
    "    \"ml.p4d.24xlarge\": 32.77   # GPU instance (8 A100 GPUs)\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Define S3 storage costs (per GB per month in USD)\n",
    "s3_costs = {\n",
    "    \"standard\": 0.023,         # S3 Standard\n",
    "    \"intelligent\": 0.0125,     # S3 Intelligent-Tiering\n",
    "    \"glacier\": 0.004           # S3 Glacier\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Define data transfer costs (per GB in USD)\n",
    "data_transfer_costs = {\n",
    "    \"s3_to_sagemaker\": 0.00,   # S3 to SageMaker (same region)\n",
    "    \"sagemaker_to_s3\": 0.00,   # SageMaker to S3 (same region)\n",
    "    \"internet_out\": 0.09       # Data transfer out to internet (first 10TB/month)\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Define model sizes (in MB)\n",
    "model_sizes = {\n",
    "    \"original\": 500,           # Original model size\n",
    "    \"quantized_int8\": 125,     # Int8 quantized model (25% of original)\n",
    "    \"quantized_fp16\": 250,     # FP16 quantized model (50% of original)\n",
    "    \"pruned_50\": 250,          # 50% pruned model\n",
    "    \"pruned_80\": 100,          # 80% pruned model\n",
    "    \"distilled\": 150,          # Knowledge distilled model\n",
    "    \"fine_tuned\": 500          # Fine-tuned model (same size as original)\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Define inference throughput (requests per second)\n",
    "inference_throughput = {\n",
    "    \"original\": 100,           # Original model\n",
    "    \"quantized_int8\": 350,     # Int8 quantized model (3.5x faster)\n",
    "    \"quantized_fp16\": 180,     # FP16 quantized model (1.8x faster)\n",
    "    \"pruned_50\": 150,          # 50% pruned model (1.5x faster)\n",
    "    \"pruned_80\": 250,          # 80% pruned model (2.5x faster)\n",
    "    \"distilled\": 200,          # Knowledge distilled model (2x faster)\n",
    "    \"fine_tuned\": 100          # Fine-tuned model (same throughput as original)\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Define model accuracy (percentage)\n",
    "model_accuracy = {\n",
    "    \"original\": 92.0,          # Original model\n",
    "    \"quantized_int8\": 90.5,    # Int8 quantized model\n",
    "    \"quantized_fp16\": 91.8,    # FP16 quantized model\n",
    "    \"pruned_50\": 91.0,         # 50% pruned model\n",
    "    \"pruned_80\": 89.0,         # 80% pruned model\n",
    "    \"distilled\": 90.0,         # Knowledge distilled model\n",
    "    \"fine_tuned\": 94.0         # Fine-tuned model\n",
    "}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Define Optimization Costs\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's define the costs associated with each optimization technique, including training time and resources required."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Define optimization costs\n",
    "optimization_costs = {\n",
    "    \"original\": {\n",
    "        \"instance_type\": \"ml.g4dn.xlarge\",\n",
    "        \"training_hours\": 0,\n",
    "        \"development_hours\": 0\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"quantized_int8\": {\n",
    "        \"instance_type\": \"ml.c5.xlarge\",\n",
    "        \"training_hours\": 2,\n",
    "        \"development_hours\": 4\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"quantized_fp16\": {\n",
    "        \"instance_type\": \"ml.c5.xlarge\",\n",
    "        \"training_hours\": 1,\n",
    "        \"development_hours\": 3\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"pruned_50\": {\n",
    "        \"instance_type\": \"ml.g4dn.xlarge\",\n",
    "        \"training_hours\": 6,\n",
    "        \"development_hours\": 8\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"pruned_80\": {\n",
    "        \"instance_type\": \"ml.g4dn.xlarge\",\n",
    "        \"training_hours\": 10,\n",
    "        \"development_hours\": 12\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"distilled\": {\n",
    "        \"instance_type\": \"ml.g4dn.2xlarge\",\n",
    "        \"training_hours\": 12,\n",
    "        \"development_hours\": 16\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"fine_tuned\": {\n",
    "        \"instance_type\": \"ml.g4dn.xlarge\",\n",
    "        \"training_hours\": 8,\n",
    "        \"development_hours\": 6\n",
    "    }\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Calculate one-time optimization costs\n",
    "for model_type, costs in optimization_costs.items():\n",
    "    instance_cost = instance_costs[costs[\"instance_type\"]]\n",
    "    training_cost = instance_cost * costs[\"training_hours\"]\n",
    "    development_cost = instance_costs[\"ml.t3.xlarge\"] * costs[\"development_hours\"]\n",
    "    total_cost = training_cost + development_cost\n",
    "    \n",
    "    optimization_costs[model_type][\"training_cost\"] = training_cost\n",
    "    optimization_costs[model_type][\"development_cost\"] = development_cost\n",
    "    optimization_costs[model_type][\"total_cost\"] = total_cost\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create a DataFrame for optimization costs\n",
    "optimization_df = pd.DataFrame([\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        \"Model Type\": model_type.replace(\"_\", \" \").title(),\n",
    "        \"Instance Type\": costs[\"instance_type\"],\n",
    "        \"Training Hours\": costs[\"training_hours\"],\n",
    "        \"Development Hours\": costs[\"development_hours\"],\n",
    "        \"Training Cost ($)\": costs[\"training_cost\"],\n",
    "        \"Development Cost ($)\": costs[\"development_cost\"],\n",
    "        \"Total Cost ($)\": costs[\"total_cost\"]\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    for model_type, costs in optimization_costs.items()\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Display the optimization costs\n",
    "print(\"One-time Optimization Costs:\")\n",
    "display(optimization_df.sort_values(\"Total Cost ($)\"))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Calculate Inference Costs\n",
    "\n",
    "Now, let's calculate the ongoing inference costs for each model type based on different throughput requirements."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Define inference scenarios\n",
    "inference_scenarios = {\n",
    "    \"low\": 50,      # 50 requests per second\n",
    "    \"medium\": 200,  # 200 requests per second\n",
    "    \"high\": 1000    # 1000 requests per second\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Define inference instance types for each model and scenario\n",
    "inference_instances = {\n",
    "    \"original\": {\n",
    "        \"low\": \"ml.g4dn.xlarge\",\n",
    "        \"medium\": \"ml.g4dn.2xlarge\",\n",
    "        \"high\": \"ml.g4dn.12xlarge\"\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"quantized_int8\": {\n",
    "        \"low\": \"ml.c5.xlarge\",\n",
    "        \"medium\": \"ml.c5.2xlarge\",\n",
    "        \"high\": \"ml.g4dn.4xlarge\"\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"quantized_fp16\": {\n",
    "        \"low\": \"ml.c5.xlarge\",\n",
    "        \"medium\": \"ml.g4dn.xlarge\",\n",
    "        \"high\": \"ml.g4dn.8xlarge\"\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"pruned_50\": {\n",
    "        \"low\": \"ml.c5.xlarge\",\n",
    "        \"medium\": \"ml.g4dn.xlarge\",\n",
    "        \"high\": \"ml.g4dn.8xlarge\"\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"pruned_80\": {\n",
    "        \"low\": \"ml.c5.xlarge\",\n",
    "        \"medium\": \"ml.c5.2xlarge\",\n",
    "        \"high\": \"ml.g4dn.4xlarge\"\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"distilled\": {\n",
    "        \"low\": \"ml.c5.xlarge\",\n",
    "        \"medium\": \"ml.c5.2xlarge\",\n",
    "        \"high\": \"ml.g4dn.4xlarge\"\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"fine_tuned\": {\n",
    "        \"low\": \"ml.g4dn.xlarge\",\n",
    "        \"medium\": \"ml.g4dn.2xlarge\",\n",
    "        \"high\": \"ml.g4dn.12xlarge\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Calculate number of instances needed for each scenario\n",
    "inference_results = {}\n",
    "\n",
    "for scenario, req_per_sec in inference_scenarios.items():\n",
    "    inference_results[scenario] = {}\n",
    "    \n",
    "    for model_type, throughput in inference_throughput.items():\n",
    "        # Calculate number of instances needed\n",
    "        instances_needed = max(1, np.ceil(req_per_sec / throughput))\n",
    "        instance_type = inference_instances[model_type][scenario]\n",
    "        hourly_cost = instance_costs[instance_type] * instances_needed\n",
    "        monthly_cost = hourly_cost * 24 * 30  # 24 hours/day, 30 days/month\n",
    "        \n",
    "        inference_results[scenario][model_type] = {\n",
    "            \"instances_needed\": instances_needed,\n",
    "            \"instance_type\": instance_type,\n",
    "            \"hourly_cost\": hourly_cost,\n",
    "            \"monthly_cost\": monthly_cost\n",
    "        }\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create DataFrames for each scenario\n",
    "for scenario, results in inference_results.items():\n",
    "    df = pd.DataFrame([\n",
    "        {\n",
    "            \"Model Type\": model_type.replace(\"_\", \" \").title(),\n",
    "            \"Instance Type\": data[\"instance_type\"],\n",
    "            \"Instances Needed\": data[\"instances_needed\"],\n",
    "            \"Hourly Cost ($)\": data[\"hourly_cost\"],\n",
    "            \"Monthly Cost ($)\": data[\"monthly_cost\"],\n",
    "            \"Accuracy (%)\": model_accuracy[model_type]\n",
    "        }\n",
    "        for model_type, data in results.items()\n",
    "    ])\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(f\"\\nInference Costs for {scenario.upper()} Traffic Scenario ({inference_scenarios[scenario]} req/sec):\")\n",
    "    display(df.sort_values(\"Monthly Cost ($)\"))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Visualize Cost Comparisons\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's create some visualizations to better understand the cost implications of different optimization techniques."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Prepare data for visualization\n",
    "scenario = \"medium\"  # Use medium traffic scenario for visualization\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create a DataFrame for monthly costs\n",
    "monthly_costs = pd.DataFrame([\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        \"Model Type\": model_type.replace(\"_\", \" \").title(),\n",
    "        \"Monthly Cost\": data[\"monthly_cost\"],\n",
    "        \"Accuracy\": model_accuracy[model_type]\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    for model_type, data in inference_results[scenario].items()\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Sort by monthly cost\n",
    "monthly_costs = monthly_costs.sort_values(\"Monthly Cost\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create a bar chart for monthly costs\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n",
    "ax = sns.barplot(x=\"Model Type\", y=\"Monthly Cost\", data=monthly_costs, palette=\"viridis\")\n",
    "plt.title(f\"Monthly Inference Costs for {scenario.title()} Traffic Scenario\", fontsize=16)\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Model Type\", fontsize=14)\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Monthly Cost ($)\", fontsize=14)\n",
    "plt.xticks(rotation=45)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add cost values on top of bars\n",
    "for i, v in enumerate(monthly_costs[\"Monthly Cost\"]):\n",
    "    ax.text(i, v + 50, f\"${v:.2f}\", ha=\"center\", fontsize=12)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create a scatter plot of cost vs. accuracy\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 8))\n",
    "sns.scatterplot(x=\"Accuracy\", y=\"Monthly Cost\", data=monthly_costs, s=200, hue=\"Model Type\", palette=\"viridis\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add model type labels to points\n",
    "for i, row in monthly_costs.iterrows():\n",
    "    plt.text(row[\"Accuracy\"] + 0.1, row[\"Monthly Cost\"], row[\"Model Type\"], fontsize=12)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.title(\"Cost vs. Accuracy Trade-off\", fontsize=16)\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Accuracy (%)\", fontsize=14)\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Monthly Cost ($)\", fontsize=14)\n",
    "plt.grid(True, linestyle=\"--\", alpha=0.7)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create a DataFrame for cumulative costs over time\n",
    "months = range(1, 37)  # 3 years\n",
    "cumulative_costs = {}\n",
    "\n",
    "for model_type in inference_results[scenario].keys():\n",
    "    monthly_cost = inference_results[scenario][model_type][\"monthly_cost\"]\n",
    "    initial_cost = 0 if model_type == \"original\" else optimization_costs[model_type][\"total_cost\"]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    cumulative_costs[model_type] = [initial_cost + (monthly_cost * month) for month in months]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create a DataFrame for plotting\n",
    "cumulative_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"Month\": list(months) * len(cumulative_costs),\n",
    "    \"Cumulative Cost\": [cost for costs in cumulative_costs.values() for cost in costs],\n",
    "    \"Model Type\": [model_type.replace(\"_\", \" \").title() for model_type in cumulative_costs.keys() for _ in months]\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create a line plot for cumulative costs\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(14, 8))\n",
    "sns.lineplot(x=\"Month\", y=\"Cumulative Cost\", hue=\"Model Type\", data=cumulative_df, linewidth=2.5)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.title(\"Cumulative Costs Over Time\", fontsize=16)\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Months\", fontsize=14)\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Cumulative Cost ($)\", fontsize=14)\n",
    "plt.grid(True, linestyle=\"--\", alpha=0.7)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add vertical lines for common break-even points\n",
    "plt.axvline(x=6, color=\"gray\", linestyle=\"--\", alpha=0.5)\n",
    "plt.text(6.2, plt.ylim()[1] * 0.9, \"6 months\", fontsize=12)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.axvline(x=12, color=\"gray\", linestyle=\"--\", alpha=0.5)\n",
    "plt.text(12.2, plt.ylim()[1] * 0.9, \"1 year\", fontsize=12)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.axvline(x=24, color=\"gray\", linestyle=\"--\", alpha=0.5)\n",
    "plt.text(24.2, plt.ylim()[1] * 0.9, \"2 years\", fontsize=12)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.legend(title=\"Model Type\", loc=\"upper left\", fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Recommendations and Conclusions\n",
    "\n",
    "Based on our cost analysis, let's summarize the key findings and provide recommendations for model optimization."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create a summary table with key metrics\n",
    "summary_data = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for model_type in [\"original\", \"quantized_int8\", \"quantized_fp16\", \"pruned_50\", \"pruned_80\", \"distilled\", \"fine_tuned\"]:\n",
    "    if model_type == \"original\":\n",
    "        roi_1year = 0\n",
    "        roi_3year = 0\n",
    "        break_even = 0\n",
    "        monthly_savings = 0\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        # Find the model in ROI results\n",
    "        model_roi = next((item for item in roi_results if item[\"Model Type\"] == model_type.replace(\"_\", \" \").title()), None)\n",
    "        if model_roi:\n",
    "            roi_1year = model_roi[\"1-Year ROI (%)\"]\n",
    "            roi_3year = model_roi[\"3-Year ROI (%)\"]\n",
    "            break_even = model_roi[\"Break-even (months)\"]\n",
    "            monthly_savings = model_roi[\"Monthly Savings ($)\"]\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            roi_1year = 0\n",
    "            roi_3year = 0\n",
    "            break_even = float('inf')\n",
    "            monthly_savings = 0\n",
    "    \n",
    "    summary_data.append({\n",
    "        \"Model Type\": model_type.replace(\"_\", \" \").title(),\n",
    "        \"Size (MB)\": model_sizes[model_type],\n",
    "        \"Size Reduction (%)\": (1 - model_sizes[model_type] / model_sizes[\"original\"]) * 100 if model_type != \"original\" else 0,\n",
    "        \"Throughput (req/sec)\": inference_throughput[model_type],\n",
    "        \"Throughput Increase (%)\": (inference_throughput[model_type] / inference_throughput[\"original\"] - 1) * 100 if model_type != \"original\" else 0,\n",
    "        \"Accuracy (%)\": model_accuracy[model_type],\n",
    "        \"Accuracy Change (%)\": model_accuracy[model_type] - model_accuracy[\"original\"] if model_type != \"original\" else 0,\n",
    "        \"Monthly Cost ($)\": inference_results[scenario][model_type][\"monthly_cost\"],\n",
    "        \"Monthly Savings ($)\": monthly_savings,\n",
    "        \"Break-even (months)\": break_even,\n",
    "        \"1-Year ROI (%)\": roi_1year,\n",
    "        \"3-Year ROI (%)\": roi_3year\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create a DataFrame for the summary\n",
    "summary_df = pd.DataFrame(summary_data)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Display the summary table\n",
    "print(\"\\nSummary of Model Optimization Techniques:\")\n",
    "display(summary_df)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Key Findings and Recommendations\n",
    "\n",
    "Based on our analysis, here are the key findings and recommendations for model optimization:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Best Overall Value: Int8 Quantization**\n",
    "   - Provides the highest throughput increase (250%)\n",
    "   - Offers significant size reduction (75%)\n",
    "   - Has minimal accuracy impact (-1.5%)\n",
    "   - Lowest implementation cost and fastest break-even point\n",
    "   - Highest ROI in both short and long term\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **Best for Accuracy-Critical Applications: Fine-tuning**\n",
    "   - Only technique that improves accuracy (+2%)\n",
    "   - No size or throughput benefits\n",
    "   - Higher implementation cost but can be justified by accuracy gains\n",
    "   - Consider combining with quantization for better cost-efficiency\n",
    "\n",
    "3. **Best for Storage Constraints: 80% Pruning**\n",
    "   - Provides the most significant size reduction (80%)\n",
    "   - Good throughput increase (150%)\n",
    "   - Higher accuracy impact (-3%)\n",
    "   - Longer implementation time but good long-term ROI\n",
    "\n",
    "4. **Best Balanced Approach: Knowledge Distillation**\n",
    "   - Good balance of size reduction (70%) and throughput increase (100%)\n",
    "   - Moderate accuracy impact (-2%)\n",
    "   - Higher implementation cost but good long-term ROI\n",
    "   - More flexible architecture options\n",
    "\n",
    "5. **Recommended Combinations:**\n",
    "   - **Fine-tuning + Int8 Quantization**: Improve accuracy first, then reduce size and increase throughput\n",
    "   - **Pruning + Quantization**: Maximize size reduction and throughput gains\n",
    "   - **Distillation + Quantization**: Create a smaller architecture, then further optimize\n",
    "\n",
    "6. **Traffic-Based Recommendations:**\n",
    "   - **Low Traffic**: Focus on reducing costs with quantization\n",
    "   - **Medium Traffic**: Balance cost and performance with distillation or pruning\n",
    "   - **High Traffic**: Prioritize throughput with quantization and consider horizontal scaling\n",
    "\n",
    "7. **Cost-Saving Strategies:**\n",
    "   - Start with quantization for quick wins\n",
    "   - Implement more complex techniques based on specific requirements\n",
    "   - Consider the trade-off between implementation cost and long-term savings\n",
    "   - Monitor performance and adjust as needed"
   ]
  },
